<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Epipolae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Epipolae is the limestone plateau that rises above the ancient city of Syracuse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. During the Athenian siege of 415–413 BCE control of the heights decided the struggle. Dionysius I then enclosed the plateau with some 27 kilometres of walls, among the longest of the Greek world, and built the fortress of Euryalus at its western end, whose remains survive.</p></div>
